`failed` is declared after `edit` but `unavailable` uses `failed()` inside the memo — the arrow function body executes lazily when accessed during render, by which time `failed` is defined in closure (const hoisting in TDZ is an issue at module init time, but the memo runs later). Actually `createMemo` may run eagerly upon creation. Solid's createMemo runs the function immediately when the computation is created (lazy evaluation? In Solid, createMemo executes once on creation? Let me recall: Solid creates the memo and computes the value lazily—actually the computation function is executed during the update phase, immediately by default? Solid's createComputation executes the function once on creation. So `unavailable` would be evaluated immediately and `failed` in TDZ → ReferenceError.

To be safe, compute failed inline in the memo. Let me fix.

